title: 'umbrella: remove test utility crates'
doc:
  - audience:
      - Node Dev
      - Runtime Dev
    description: |
      The `polkadot-sdk` umbrella crate no longer includes `asset-test-utils`,
      `bridge-hub-test-utils`, `emulated-integration-tests-common` and
      `parachains-runtimes-test-utils`. The `node` feature enabled these crates. They pulled
      `assets-common` and `pallet-revive` into each node that uses the umbrella. With
      `runtime-benchmarks`, they also built `pallet-revive-fixtures`.

      These crates are still published. If you use them through the umbrella, add them as
      direct dependencies.
crates:
  - name: polkadot-sdk
    bump: major
  - name: asset-test-utils
    bump: none
  - name: bridge-hub-test-utils
    bump: none
  - name: emulated-integration-tests-common
    bump: none
  - name: parachains-runtimes-test-utils
    bump: none
